# Tools UI

Catalog source of truth: `src/lib/tools.ts` (`id`, `name`, `description`, `icon`, `category`, `popular`).
Home directory lives on `/` (`HomePageClient`) — there is no separate `/tools` route, sidebar, sort control, or grid/list toggle. Do not add those unless asked. `src/components/ui/sidebar.tsx` is a shadcn primitive, not a tools nav.

Visual tokens: follow the design-system rule / `globals.css`. Do not invent a second look.

## Directory (existing)

- Search: `ToolSearch` + `InputGroup`. Placeholder “Search tools, calculators, converters…”. No keyboard-shortcut search exists — do not invent one or a second search stack
- Category pills from `HomePageClient`: All Tools, Financial, Health, Date & Time, Math, Conversion, Planning, Utility (counts from catalog)
- `tools.ts` also has AI Tools, Security, Business — only show categories the UI actually supports; do not invent Calculators / Fun / Developer
- Featured/popular: `popular: true` via `FeaturedTools` / ⭐ Popular badge. Do not fabricate usage numbers

## Tool card

Keep one component structure (`ToolGrid` / `FeaturedTools`). When adding or restyling:

1. Lucide icon (pastel well when restyling)
2. Category badge
3. Tool name
4. Short description
5. Popular badge only if `popular`
6. Clear action (link to `/{id}`; “Use Tool” copy only if adding a CTA)
7. Chevron

Do not overcrowd. Do not invent trending/usage stats.

## Tool pages

Pattern: `src/app/{id}/page.tsx` shell + `src/components/tools/{id}.tsx` (or `Image-tools/`).

Existing shell: gradient title, muted subtitle, “Back to Home”, `Card` wrapping the tool. Keep that ecosystem.

Prefer: title, short explanation, inputs, results, validation/errors (sonner/inline), reset where it already exists (e.g. GST), related tools only if adding them from `tools.ts`. Responsive: stack on mobile; `lg:grid-cols-2` input | result where already used.

Do not redesign calculation logic while changing UI.

## Financial / math

Reuse `calculateEMI`, `calculateAge`, `formatCurrency`, `formatNumber` in `src/lib/utils.ts`. EMI/GST precision and INR/`en-IN` formatting stay as-is. Formulas live in the tool components — do not “simplify” for visuals. No test suite yet; if you change calc behavior, add tests.

Client-only tools: persist via existing `getFromStorage` / `setToStorage` helpers where already used (todo, goals). Do not add a backend for calculators.
